On Wed, 13 Jul 2011, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> I may be misunderstanding you patch, but it seems not really necessary
> because there are so many ways to move, not only the ordinary [prefixed]
> single moves but - besides the "complex" travel command - also the
> g-prefixed moves. Actually, the <g>-<dir> sequence is the variant of
> move that I seem to constantly use in all the predominant cases where
I know about 'g', and often use it when I encounter what appears to be a
boring long corridor during initial exploration.

> I move more than a single square. The travel command, BTW, is useful on
> explored levels (only?), and it can be made significantly less "complex"

But explored levels are mostly the problem.  Basically I'm only
comfortable doing the routing myself (so no '_'), but part of my brain
precalculates the route and spools it out to the game via the keyboard
just a bit faster than the other part can notice a monster appearing out
of the darkness. Bumplock definitively halts my spooler so the rest of my
brain can catch up.

> For keep-your-fingers-on-a-key-to-move-many-squares players your patch
You mean holding down a key until it repeats?  That's just crazy.

